# Milestone: W4/v0.10.2
# Covers: Tag.new("name") creates a UVAL_TAG value; tag scope body runs when
#         the tag expression evaluates to a UVAL_TAG (not just nil/int);
#         two Tag.new() calls produce distinct tags (pointer-identity check).
# Activated: v0.10.2-reactive W4 (UVAL_TAG + Tag.new() constructor).
#
# Note: the original M3 draft tested variable-scoping isolation using Tag.new()
# (var t = Tag.new() | {t: var foo = 42; foo} expecting lookup-failed: foo).
# That test remains deferred to W5 because it requires the bare-label `t:`
# to BIND the scope's anonymous UTag to `t` (OP_PUSH_TAG W5 register hook).
# What IS testable now: Tag.new() creates a real UVAL_TAG, tag scopes work
# with UVAL_TAG identifiers, and two tags are distinct objects.

var t1 = Tag.new("a")
var t2 = Tag.new("b")
t1
t2
t1 == t1
t1 == t2
var x = 0; t1: { x = 99 }; x
[00000000] <Tag: a>
[00000001] <Tag: b>
[00000002] <Tag: a>
[00000003] <Tag: b>
[00000004] true
[00000005] false
[00000006] 99
